//
// The LM-head GEMV's re-execution gate. The research branch found (doc 57
// section 1.4, devq 446-448, 452, 458) that the 19 x 8192 `lm_head_gemv`
// multi-launch ELF returned wrong, non-deterministic values in partition 0
// whenever it executed immediately after itself: 5 of 7 dispatches wrong,
// healed by running another ELF in between but NOT by a 0.5 s idle.
// Production decode never places the head next to itself and `make verify`
// judges token sets, so neither could see it.
//
// The family is understood: an ODD per-dispatch LOAD_PDI count ends on the
// empty reset PDI the next dispatch starts with, the NPU2 firmware skips that
// load, and launch 0 runs on the previous dispatch's DMA/lock state. The
// compiler pads odd dispatches, and the branch recorded the 19 x 8192 form
// re-executing clean once it did (devq 534).
//
// This gate is that check, on main. Main still ships the 19 x 8192 geometry,
// and it reads 7/7 clean here (devq 934, and devq 935 with the control), which
// confirms main carries the padding fix rather than being green by partition
// parity. It is a regression guard: a builder or compiler change that brings
// the family back turns this red.
//
// The first line checked is a deliberately corrupted vector that the same
// judge must reject. Without it a clean verdict would only mean the judge
// never says WRONG.
//
// No HF weights: random weights against an f32 reference. NPU serialization
// lives one layer down (KernelCache takes /tmp/npu.lock).
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_lm_head_reexec
// RUN: cd test_npu2_lm_head_reexec
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-lm-head-reexec PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// CHECK: [reexec] c0 CONTROL (deliberately corrupted): WRONG
// CHECK: [reexec] d1 first dispatch: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d2 back-to-back: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d3 back-to-back: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d4 after 0.5 s idle: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d5 new input back-to-back: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d6 after other ELF: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d7 back-to-back after d6: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] PASS
